- All requests require the dLazy API key via CLI configuration.
- **CLI Configuration**: You can set your API key using the following command:
- The API key is stored locally in plaintext at `~/.dlazy/config.json` (Windows: `%USERPROFILE%\.dlazy\config.json`). You can also pass it ephemerally via the `DLAZY_API_KEY` environment variable instead of persisting it.
- 3. Click the copy button on the right side of API Key section to copy it
- We recommend using a least-privilege / per-project key that you can rotate or revoke at any time.
- ## Data & Privacy
- When this skill runs, the following data leaves your machine:
- - **Prompts and parameters** you pass via CLI flags are sent to dLazy backend (`dlazy.com` / `api.dlazy.com`).
- - **Local file paths** supplied to image / video / audio fields are read from disk and uploaded to dLazy storage (`oss.dlazy.com`) so the model can access them.
- - **Generated outputs** (URLs returned in the JSON response) are hosted on `oss.dlazy.com`.
- Do not pass files containing secrets, personally identifying information, or other content you are not authorized to share with dLazy. Review dLazy's privacy policy at [dlazy.com](https://dlazy.com) before sending sensitive material.
